00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:10.880
I think a positive home environment,
just, it just can make all the difference.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.300
You know, I mean, if I think of a young
person that I worked with, who, who

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:21.873
came to me with quite crippling anxiety
really, but mum and dad were very present.

00:00:21.903 --> 00:00:23.283
They were bringing him to his sessions.

00:00:23.283 --> 00:00:27.038
They were doing some of the
work that I sent him away with.

00:00:27.406 --> 00:00:30.361
They were together, very happy
family by the sounds of things.

00:00:30.361 --> 00:00:35.044
And I think he was able to recover
so quickly just by taking on

00:00:35.044 --> 00:00:38.524
the information that I gave him
and sharing it with his family.

00:00:38.648 --> 00:00:43.830
He was -  he just changed so much in
six weeks because I think it wasn't

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.290
only the sessions that were helping him.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.730
He then had that outside.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:52.129
And I think within that positive sort of
reinforcement at home and that sense of

00:00:52.129 --> 00:00:55.099
sort of togetherness -  and it's really
hard because so many families can't be

00:00:55.099 --> 00:00:58.609
together - and so many of the families,
you know, the majority of the young

00:00:58.609 --> 00:01:03.989
people that I support, there is some
sort of issues at home, I would say.

00:01:04.509 --> 00:01:08.484
So it's rare  that we see ones where
everything's really positive, positive

00:01:08.484 --> 00:01:11.044
at home, even if there's just one
parent at home and you've got really

00:01:11.044 --> 00:01:12.754
good trusting relationship with them.

00:01:13.384 --> 00:01:14.854
I think it can be the difference.

00:01:15.124 --> 00:01:19.864
One of the biggest things about having
a positive situation at home is that

00:01:19.874 --> 00:01:25.144
when you finish your support with a
mental health worker, it doesn't stop,

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:29.314
in a way, because parents are very
invested and there's stability at home.

00:01:29.374 --> 00:01:32.278
So I think, you know, they can continue
if they feel they can continue to

00:01:32.278 --> 00:01:34.228
talk about what's going on for them.

00:01:34.348 --> 00:01:37.918
You know, this young person I was talking
about it, for example, if he can then

00:01:37.918 --> 00:01:43.328
say six weeks after our sessions finished
that "oh feeling anxious again", then

00:01:43.328 --> 00:01:46.728
his mum and dad can sort of return
him to the work he did with me without

00:01:46.738 --> 00:01:48.988
having to refer him for more support.

00:01:49.468 --> 00:01:50.548
So, yeah, I think it's...

00:01:50.594 --> 00:01:56.223
it doesn't mean that you can't have
those results in someone whose life

00:01:56.253 --> 00:02:00.693
is a bit less stable, but I think it's
a really good sort of starting block

00:02:00.723 --> 00:02:02.373
if you've got that stability at home.

